WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.769
-My next guest
executive-produces and stars in

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.271
the big, new reboot of "iCarly"!

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.840
[ Cheers and applause ]
I'm mad about "iCarly."

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.777
You can see new episodes every
Thursday on Paramount+.

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:15.014
Please welcome Miranda Cosgrove!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:18.617
- ♪ Miranda Cosgrove,
she's flyin' high ♪

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.453
♪ America's sweetheart ♪

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.822
♪ And Carly with an "I" ♪

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.691
♪ I got more questions ♪

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.525
♪ And get you to say no ♪

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:28.194
-Miranda Cosgrove.
Look at that, come on.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.129
Look.
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.265
We love you.
-Thank you.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.967
-Miranda, welcome to the show.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.134
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.770
I'm so excited to be here.
-We love you.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.706
Actually, we've worked together.
-Yes.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.109
-I was so happy to be on
an episode of "iCarly."

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.644
But I want to -- I want to talk
to you all about that.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.480
But, first, I don't know
if you've noticed this,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.915
but you've kind of become
the queen of memes.

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.751
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.919
It's true. My legacy.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.321
-Your legacy.
-The queen of memes.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.624
-Yeah, since you were -- How old
were you when you first started?

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.359
-Meming?
-Yeah.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.627
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.927
You didn't even know
you were meming at the time.

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:04.130
-I think the first meme
that became popular of me,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.932
I was 8 or 9.
-Yeah, 8 years old.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.735
And I have a couple of them
because I want to show everyone

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.803
in case you need a good meme.
-Oh, boy.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.573
-Here's one that says,
"When they finally play

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.607
Sum 41 'Fatlip'
at the house party."

00:01:15.607 --> 00:01:17.977
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:21.781
-I was obsessed with doing this,
and I really paid for it.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.215
Like, I just couldn't stop
doing that.

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.584
-It's so cute.
Are you kidding me?

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.752
Come on, like, "Nice try."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:30.790
I like this one, too.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.793
This is interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.628
"Seeing your friend
tweet someone they 'hate.'"

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.230
"Interesting."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.766
"Interesting."
You made the "interesting" face.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.001
And then what I thought
was funny is

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.770
that the new "iCarly,"
the reboot,

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.708
you redid the "interesting" face
as a joke,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.477
and that became a meme.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:53.213
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.914
-It took on a life of its own.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.283
-New interesting.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.751
It's got a life of its own.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.820
-You reunited
with the cast of "iCarly."

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.489
Did you know you were
going to do the reboot,

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.958
or were you just supposed
to just show up

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.060
for, like, one episode reunion,
or how did you...

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.095
-We knew we were gonna do
the revival,

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:12.498
and we were super excited,
but we got a call

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.167
to all go to this event
and we were supposed to

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.003
announce it together that we
were gonna be doing a revival.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.771
So, my friend, Jerry Trainor,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.873
who plays my brother
on "iCarly" --

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.942
-I love Jerry.
-He's the best.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.244
So, he called me up
and he was like, "You know,

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:29.482
with COVID, we've been inside.
We could use some sun."

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.484
He was like, "I know you've
gotten a spray tan before.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.119
Do you think
you could hook me up,

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.221
and the two of us could get
a spray tan together?"

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.855
So, I was like, "Okay."

00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:38.424
Like, it's so out of character
for Jerry.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.793
I didn't expect it at all.
-Yeah, that's --

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.161
-So I said, "Sure, yeah."
So we went,

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.664
we got the spray tan together,
and then the next morning

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.899
was the event,
and I didn't hear from him.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.501
I kept texting him,
"How's it going?"

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.768
Like, "Do you like
how it turned out?"

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:50.970
I wasn't hearing from him.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.871
So, then,
the way spray tans work,

00:02:52.871 --> 00:02:54.506
if you -- I don't know
if you've ever had one,

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:57.442
but if you get one,
it keeps developing

00:02:57.442 --> 00:02:59.545
until you wash it off.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:02.781
So, he fell asleep, and
he never washed it off.

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:05.051
And the next morning,
I brought --

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.153
This is a picture for you.
This is what happened.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:10.222
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:13.359
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.594
It's pretty bad.
-Dude, look at that.

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:18.197
Oh, my gosh.
It looks like he's burnt.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:21.100
-I love this picture.
I had it as my wallpaper

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.235
on my phone for a long time.
Anytime I'm sad,

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.938
I look at this picture
and it makes me feel so good.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.374
-He looks like -- He looks like
the color of the blimp.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.476
-He's Nickelodeon orange.
-He's Nickelodeon orange.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:33.679
Yeah, that's what he went with.
Was he -- Was he mad?

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:36.315
-So, he was very upset,
and he blamed me.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:39.752
And then, later, we were filming
an episode for the show,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.820
and in the episode,
I'm supposed to make

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.089
this kind of crazy,
hideous face.

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:47.060
And it's turn into
this giant Andy Warhol-type

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.262
piece of art in the episode.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.297
So he asked if he
could take it home

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.598
when we finished the episode

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.967
and he put it up in his house
to get me back.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.837
-Here's the piece of art.
-That's the piece of art.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.672
I'm supposed to be
eating a meatball.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.906
[ Laughter ]
-That's that.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:03.676
And then here's Jerry with you.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.012
-And showing it to me
is his revenge.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.414
-In his living room.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.916
I love it.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.051
Please send -- send my regards
to the whole cast.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.786
People are loving this reboot,
by the way.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.188
-Thank you.
-100% fresh on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:18.257
100%. It's awesome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.492
-Thank you.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.327
It already got renewed
for season two.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.829
Where does it pick up, this?
-It's pretty much

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.697
eight years
after the old one ended.

00:04:25.697 --> 00:04:27.099
It's just
all the same characters

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.433
and what they're
going through now.

00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:30.769
Now that we're older, and
it's a much more mature take.

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:33.306
We're doing stuff in this one
we couldn't do in the old.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:37.477
-Yeah, and the audience
for this, is it --

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:39.478
they're not kids now.
-No, it's really for

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:40.980
the original audience
that's grown-up.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.849
-Yeah, that's brilliant,
and it works.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:45.051
You figured it out.
That's awesome.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:47.086
It's worth -- I want to show
a clip right now.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.589
Here is Miranda Cosgrove
in "iCarly."

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.157
Take a look.

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.426
-Freddie, just hand me
that, uh, twisty thingy.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.662
[ Laughter ]
Okay, this is no big deal.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:57.563
-Alright.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.532
-Aah!

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.166
Ow!
-Hey!

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:03.635
I got ya. Come on!
-Aah!

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:06.606
Son of a [Horn honks]

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:09.642
-You know what? That's okay.
I've almost got it.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.377
Freddie, go check
the spark plugs.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.211
-Alright.
-Millicent, start 'em up!

00:05:13.211 --> 00:05:15.247
[ Engine sputtering ]

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:17.482
-Oh!
[ Horn honks ]

00:05:17.482 --> 00:05:19.619
-Millicent, stop that!

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:22.021
-Then you two stop cussing.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.457
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.692
-Ah. We're down, buddy.
Miranda Cosgrove.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.794
Check out new episodes
of "iCarly"

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.396
every Thursday on Paramount+.

